If you then let that mouse grow up, and in the case of a mouse, that's not 18 years, that's 20 weeks or so. and you put the mouse back in that same maze, they won't remember how to escape. That is, they show something like infantal amnesia. They don't remember something they learned early in their life. So the recent research, though, used very fancy modern molecular methods to figure out how the initial infant mouse's memory had been stored.
