involved in storing reward-related memories. And so really when you're measuring an infant's behavior, you don't know which of these brain structures or perhaps other developing brain structures might be responsible for what infants can start remembering. And so our research using functional MRI was able to look under the hood and say, what's happening in a baby's brain when memories are being formed? And we focused on the hippocampus in particular because it's deep in the brain. It's in adults, the only way to access it, you know, through brain imaging is with functional MRI. A part of my lab focuses on adults.
所以当你测量婴儿的行为时，你不知道这些大脑结构中的哪一个，或者其他正在发育的大脑结构，可能对婴儿开始记住的东西负责。因此，我们使用功能性磁共振成像（fMRI）的研究能够深入内部，观察婴儿大脑在形成记忆时发生了什么。我们特别关注海马体，因为它位于大脑深处。在成年人中，通过脑成像访问它的唯一方法是使用功能性磁共振成像。我的实验室的一部分专注于成人。

